{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The cleaning cloth fits with my recent blower duster purchase because both help me maintain my laptop and workspace.",
    "The surge protector fits my desk and cable organization, while the USB flash drive would help me move files and prepare installation media for computer and Raspberry Pi projects."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Another HDMI cable or pair of headphones repeats equipment I already have without addressing a new need; my recent headphone mount suggests organizing what I own.",
    "The streaming stick, smart speaker, and tablet do not help with the wired networking and workspace tasks I am focused on, and the RAM requires compatibility information I have not confirmed."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Owning electronics seems to have been taken as a reason to suggest more entertainment devices, even though my recent purchases serve practical setup and maintenance needs.",
    "My past cable and headphone purchases seem to have been treated as ongoing demand for more of the same, rather than needs I may already have met."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent Ethernet adapter, network cables, headphone mount, and blower duster point toward improving and maintaining an existing workspace.",
    "Useful additions should complement equipment I already own, and hardware upgrades need a clear fit with my devices and an actual reason to upgrade."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my practical computer needs but too often interpreted electronics ownership as a reason to add more devices."
}"}
